  CONSEQUENCE.  w_max grows LINEARLY in l = L while W_L stays below 16/3, so a
  seed-independent bound  w_max <= K log2(l) + C  is FALSE for complete finite
  positive-orbit episodes.  This REFUTES the (DEPTH-DURATION) lemma proposed at
  the end of the previous round.  The cost appears instead in the seed:
  m_0 >= 2^{L+4} - 3, i.e. log2 m_0 >= L + 4 - o(1) -- linear in the depth.
  It does NOT refute the statement restricted to globally divergent orbits:
  these seeds reach 1, so by Rev 8 Lemma 4.2 their drift tends to +infinity.

